+# C5 verdict-change evidence: candidate status
+
+Recorded: 2026-10-21T20:41:00Z
+Status: **NOT RUN on this candidate.**
+
+## Why the old C5 evidence is not reused
+
+The published branch `engine/od-scope-v25` carries
+`evidence/engine/c5/v24-pinned-old-c78.json`,
+`v24-pinned-new-od-scope.json`, and related files. They compare the
+superseded `c78` lineage against a working tree, not `main` against this
+candidate. They also embed absolute local temporary paths and an
+`outdir` that is not reproducible from the repository. They are preserved
+as historical evidence only.
+
+## Required comparison
+
+- Old: `main` @ `63da0e347002ed9b77071ff1ed0cefda7c0ce88a`
+- New: the commit containing this note
+- Method: detached Git worktrees at the exact SHAs; one common driver;
+  `PYTHONPATH=<worktree>/backend`; no working-tree comparison.
+- Inputs: v24 `coordinate_manifest.json` bytes verified against
+  `9722c3e45d316ff58ed326df074eec138b81ceb520191a492088cc0ddef63762`.
+- Binding: v24 `run_manifest.json` bytes verified against
+  `f602351f4844531d409cfc256939508103e3c2d4f57fe21d7f77c34494aa4036`.
+- Output: per-target old/new verdict, changed law rows, sample counts,
+  coverage bases, and raw-measurement digests.
+- Evidence: repo-relative paths only; exact commands; environment; input
+  and output SHA-256; no local absolute paths.
+- Failure states: the 10 unavailable v24 predictions remain explicit
+  failures; they must not be replaced or counted as PASS.
+
+## Cohort reality
+
+The v24 manifest has 50 targets. Only 40 coordinate files were acquired
+and byte-verified; 10 AlphaFold `model_v4` URLs returned HTTP 404:
+
+`AF-O15111-F1`, `AF-P00533-F1`, `AF-P02768-F1`, `AF-P04637-F1`,
+`AF-P0DTC2-F1`, `AF-P10636-F1`, `AF-P21802-F1`, `AF-P62988-F1`,
+`AF-P68871-F1`, and `AF-Q9Y6K9-F1`.
+
+A separate 9-target AlphaFold v6 supplementary set exists on the old
+branch. It is not the pinned v24 cohort and must be reported separately.
+No v25 calibration or held-out evaluation is authorized.
+
+## Acceptance for the C5 artifact
+
+1. Both engine SHAs are recorded in full.
+2. Every coordinate file is byte-verified before measurement.
+3. The 40/50 v24 availability and the 10 explicit failures are reported.
+4. The old/new comparison uses identical thresholds and ingestion.
+5. Every changed verdict has a reproducible raw-measurement file and
+   digest.
+6. Experimental structures show no pLDDT scope change; any predicted
+   structure shows law rows with explicit atom counts.
+7. The artifact contains no absolute local paths.
+8. The artifact is committed with the candidate, not before it.
+
+## Expected shape (not a result)
+
+The old C5 report found 0/40 verdict changes for the v24 experimental
+cohort, because experimental structures retain all atoms. It also found
+heuristic `LAW-182`/`LAW-200` raw VETOs becoming advisory failures. Those
+historical observations are not a prediction for this candidate; the new
+harness must produce its own results.
