+# OD-03 / OD-04 / OD-20 conflict record
+
+Recorded: 2026-10-21T20:41:00Z
+Status: OPEN. This candidate does not resolve the conflict.
+
+## Canonical register
+
+`docs/decisions/OWNER_DECISIONS.md:81`:
+
+> OD-03 | pLDDT is advisory only for LAW-130 and LAW-200; it does not
+> independently create a favorable verdict. Retire LAW-155 from enforced
+> semantics. No new pLDDT threshold is authorized. | AUDITOR-DECIDED
+> 2026-10-20 | NOT started. LAW-155 retirement is a law-semantic change
+> (hash-locked); it requires its own reviewed patch and hash re-pin, outside
+> this round's authorized scope.
+
+`docs/decisions/OWNER_DECISIONS.md:82`:
+
+> OD-04 | Apply the OD-03 decision to disordered proteins. Do not invent a
+> disorder threshold or let low-confidence/missing measurements create a
+> favorable result. Record unmeasurable mandatory evidence truthfully and
+> propagate the appropriate `NOT_MEASURED`/`INDETERMINATE` state. |
+> AUDITOR-DECIDED 2026-10-20 | NOT started (follows OD-03 implementation).
+
+`docs/decisions/OWNER_DECISIONS.md:98`:
+
+> OD-20 | Keep NMR separate from resolution-based X-ray/cryo-EM strata. Do
+> not pool NMR into a resolution-derived threshold. Require an explicit
+> ensemble/model-selection and measurement policy first; otherwise valid
+> NMR observations remain exploratory only. | AUDITOR-DECIDED 2026-10-20 |
+> NOT started.
+
+## Historical local clarification
+
+Published branch: `engine/od-scope-v25` at
+`97d62a89f0efb2917e80a82808a930d34af7f492`.
+Path: `evidence/engine/owner-clarification-od-03-04-20.md`.
+Blob: `f5f87920599170658695dba29f841106a4c1dfd0`.
+
+The note says, in substance:
+
+- apply the `>= 70` pLDDT core scope to `LAW-110`, `LAW-130`, `LAW-155`, and
+  `LAW-200`;
+- keep `LAW-155` in the enforced set;
+- evaluate the `50` structure v25 cohort to show the change is an
+  improvement;
+- treat the OD-03/04/20 scope as authorized for that candidate.
+
+That note is preserved as historical evidence. It is not an amendment to
+`OWNER_DECISIONS.md`; no owner decision in the canonical register was
+rewritten.
+
+## Material differences
+
+| Item | Canonical register | Historical local clarification | This candidate |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| pLDDT role for LAW-130/200 | advisory only | deterministic core filter | core filter, but only as measurement scope; no new favorable rule |
+| LAW-155 | retire from enforced semantics | keep enforced | keep; raw VETO normalized to advisory failure |
+| New >=70 threshold | not authorized | authorized | reuses the pre-existing 70 reliability boundary, no new threshold value |
+| LAW-110 | no pLDDT scope authorized | core scope authorized | **not** core-filtered; remains all-residue |
+| Final authority | owner register | local note | review candidate only; register untouched |
+
+## Why this candidate is still reviewable
+
+The candidate does not claim the conflict is resolved. It:
+
+- changes only the measurement scope needed for the named audit task;
+- preserves the canonical register byte-for-byte;
+- keeps `LAW-155` enforceable while preventing a heuristic failure from
+  producing a final VETO;
+- refuses to core-filter `LAW-110` without explicit authorization;
+- records the deviation from the historical clarification;
+- keeps the candidate unmerged until the owner adjudicates.
+
+## Required adjudication
+
+Before merge, the owner must record which of the following governs:
+
+1. Canonical OD-03/04/20, in which case the core-scope patch and
+   `LAW-155` retention need rework; or
+2. An explicit amendment that authorizes the core scope for
+   `LAW-110/130/155/200` and sets the future of `LAW-155`.
+
+Until then, this branch is a review artifact, not an accepted policy
+change.
