+# Policy and semantic diff record
+
+Recorded: 2026-10-21T20:41:00Z
+Baseline: `main` @ `63da0e347002ed9b77071ff1ed0cefda7c0ce88a`
+
+## Hash locks
+
+| Lock | Baseline `main` | Candidate | Status |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `LAW_CANON_HASH` (`station_sop.py`) | `6a9cd4b4349b81de` | `6a9cd4b4349b81de` | unchanged |
+| Modality matrix hash | `ed1731ace09a9a3bd24d3659ab6f3fd184da2a2335d935a234fd6a9c14880aa4` | same | unchanged |
+| `governance/law_registry.sha256` | `d53a2a506f4ddff8e7210489afc55bea60e137e2f516c3192b1e3fa5ade1d7ae` | `c09439cd2f0f4103a1c794839846f40fa45e46337481684380152ff4feaff098` | intentionally re-pinned |
+| `governance/law_semantic.sha256` | absent on `main` | absent | not added |
+
+`main` has no semantic-hash mechanism, no `governance/law_semantic.sha256`,
+and no `backend/tests/test_law_semantic_hash.py`. This patch does not add
+that science-line feature.
+
+The published `engine/od-scope-v25` lineage carried a semantic pin
+`3f49a7b5605e17dcf26bcd114713ad651cdc2279d684f1c681943eefa0f4379a` ->
+`4532a073225e98cb0094d7301591e9fe4d830b07169e670c9eb7d0deab561bbe`
+in its large `360373d` patch, and a registry pin of
+`7e3b42d59feeca5501001f702eab7d6af0a83f6855c5d3ec2e474840c0f23e93`.
+Those values describe a different tree and a much larger semantic change.
+They are not copied into this candidate.
+
+## Registry changes
+
+The registry pin changes because the machine-readable policy text changes.
+The change is limited to:
+
+| Law | Field | Before | After |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| LAW-105 | `measures` | residue coverage governs the PASS/INDETERMINATE gate | parsed-residue coverage is reported; the global gate uses atom coverage |
+| LAW-130 | `scope` | `total atoms` | `core atoms` |
+| LAW-130 | `measures` | clashes per 1000 atoms, all atoms | clashes per 1000 core atoms; experimental uses all selected atoms |
+| LAW-155 | `scope` | `atomic grid` | `core atomic grid` |
+| LAW-155 | `measures` | voxels per residue over an atomic grid | voxels per core residue over the core atomic grid |
+| LAW-200 | `scope` | `bounding box` | `core bounding box` |
+| LAW-200 | `measures` | bounding-box volume / atom count | core bounding-box volume / core atom count |
+
+No threshold value, operator, law ID, unit, or type changed. The canon hash
+covers the `LAW_CANON` table; it is unchanged because scope strings are not
+part of that table's hash input.
+
+## Engine semantics
+
+1. `LAW-105.observed` remains parsed-residue coverage. It is not silently
+   redefined as atom coverage.
+2. The returned global coverage changes from residue coverage to atom
+   coverage. This is the OD-04 gate; a 75% residue / 50% atom structure is
+   `INDETERMINATE`.
+3. `LAW-130`, `LAW-155`, and `LAW-200` use core atoms for predicted
+   structures. Experimental structures use all parsed atoms.
+4. Empty core is `NOT_MEASURED`, not `PASS` and not a zero-valued
+   measurement.
+5. `LAW-110` is unchanged and remains all-residue. It is not core-filtered.
+6. `LAW-130` remains `< 20.0` (strict). The `<=` / KDTree-failure fix is a
+   separate branch and is not part of this semantic state.
+7. A raw heuristic `VETO` is normalized to `FAIL (Advisory)` and cannot
+   produce a final VETO. This is a status-semantics repair, not a law
+   retirement or threshold change.
+
+## Why the registry re-pin is legitimate
+
+The registry text is part of the policy surface. Leaving the old pin would
+make the hash-lock test pass against stale text and would hide a
+scientific-semantic change. The new pin is computed over the exact new
+`governance/law_registry.yaml` bytes:
+
+```powershell
+(Get-FileHash governance/law_registry.yaml -Algorithm SHA256).Hash.ToLower()
+```
+
+The test constant and `governance/law_registry.sha256` carry the same
+value. This is a deliberate policy change, recorded here and in the
+canonical conflict record; it is not a hash bypass.
+
+## Reproduce the lock check
+
+```powershell
+$env:PYTHONPATH = "backend"
+python -m pytest backend/tests/test_law_registry.py -q
+python -c "from tos.governance.station_sop import LAW_CANON_HASH; print(LAW_CANON_HASH)"
+python -c "import tos.governance.modality_matrix as m; print(m.compute_matrix_hash())"
+```
